90)91000-z.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1016/0140-6736(90)91000-z"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="1970028"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=Lancet&amp;title=Hypothesis: does breast cancer originate in utero?&amp;author=D. Trichopoulos&amp;volume=335&amp;publication_year=1990&amp;pages=939-940&amp;pmid=1970028&amp;doi=10.1016/0140-6736(90)91000-z&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="BIB21"><label>21.</label><mixed-citation id="reference0100"><named-content content-type="citation-string">Hilakivi-Clarke L., Clarke R., Onojafe I., Raygada M., Cho B., Lippman M. maternal diet high in n-6 polyunsaturated fats alters mammary gland development, puberty onset, and breast cancer risk among female rat offspring. Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA. 1997;94:9372–9377. doi: 10.1073/pnas.94.17.9372.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1073/pnas.94.17.9372"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmcid" xlink:href="PMC23197"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="9256489"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA&amp;title=maternal diet high in n-6 polyunsaturated fats alters mammary gland development, puberty onset, and breast cancer risk among female rat offspring&amp;author=L. Hilakivi-Clarke&amp;author=R. Clarke&amp;author=I. Onojafe&amp;author=M. Raygada&amp;author=B. Cho&amp;volume=94&amp;publication_year=1997&amp;pages=9372-9377&amp;pmid=9256489&amp;doi=10.1073/pnas.94.17.9372&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="BIB22"><label>22.</label><mixed-citation id="reference0105"><named-content content-type="citation-string">Welsch C.W. Host factors affecting the growth of carcinogen-induced rat mammary carcinomas: a review and tribute to Charles Brenton Huggins. Cancer Res. 1985;45:3415–3443.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="3926298"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=Cancer Res.&amp;title=Host factors affecting the growth of carcinogen-induced rat mammary carcinomas: a review and tribute to Charles Brenton Huggins&amp;author=C.W. Welsch&amp;volume=45&amp;publication_year=1985&amp;pages=3415-3443&amp;pmid=3926298&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="BIB23"><label>23.</label><mixed-citation id="reference0110"><named-content content-type="citation-string">Cardiff R.D. Are the TDLU of the human the same as the LA of mice? J. Mamm. Gland Biol. Neopl. 1998;3:3–5. doi: 10.1023/a:1018714016205.</named-content><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1023/a:1018714016205"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="pmid" xlink:href="10819500"/><ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="google-scholar" xlink:href="journal=J. Mamm. Gland Biol. Neopl.&amp;title=Are the TDLU of the human the same as the LA of mice?&amp;author=R.D. Cardiff&amp;volume=3&amp;publication_year=1998&amp;pages=3-5&amp;pmid=10819500&amp;doi=10.1023/a:1018714016205&amp;"/></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></sec></sec></body></article>